Smart_Sensors
Sensors are to monitor daily activity at home, learn a person's usual routines, and alert authorised caregivers or relatives 
when significant changes are detected.
 It can record when the monitored entrance opens or closes, helping caregivers understand when the person leaves or returns, depending on the sensor setup.
 sensors also help to notice change in bathroom visits, especially at night, may indicate if patient is diebetic so  marked on app or a change in routine or sleep pattern.
if door remains open it alarms untill door is closed.
